# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# Chairman ruling R7, 15 September 2026: "ship the four headers and short
# HSTS; CSP is a separate item." The four content/referrer/frame/permissions
# headers have no lock-in on a static site. HSTS is deliberately short
# (7 days) with no preload and no includeSubDomains for the first rollout;
# lengthen it once a cycle has passed without incident. No
# Content-Security-Policy here, report-only or enforced, until the inline
# script inventory (theme toggle, nav script, Pagefind UI) is known — that
# is its own T3 item. `npm run audit:static` lints this file.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=604800

/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
